## CURRENT STATE

- `frontend/` + `backend/` remain the served product. The public Netlify
  `frontend-next/` beta is separate and is not the Phase 13 cutover.
- Migration numbering is authoritative: Phase 11 = admitted AI extensions,
  Phase 12 = Club/Community, Phase 13 = Cutover.
- Personal profile photos ship on `main` via PR from `feature/profile-photo`,
  an explicitly admitted named exception. The six curated preset avatars
  remain available.
- Prepared photos are decoded in the browser, center-cropped, resized to
  512 x 512 and freshly encoded as WebP at quality 0.86. Input is limited to
  JPEG, PNG or WebP and 5 MB; re-encoding decoded pixels removes original
  EXIF and other source metadata.
- Stored custom-avatar references use the canonical form
  `<profile-uuid>/<object-uuid>.webp`. Persistence and rendering accept a
  custom reference only when its owner folder matches the declaring profile;
  arbitrary, external, foreign-owner and malformed values fail closed.
- The Account page has local pre-save preview, upload/replace/remove controls,
  preset and initials transitions, loading states, readable errors and separate
  cleanup warnings. The public listing detail renders the validated seller photo
  or falls back to initials.
- Migration `20260821183000_profile_avatars.sql` creates the public-read
  `avatar-profili` bucket, limits objects to WebP and 5 MB, restricts writes to
  the authenticated user's canonical folder and constrains `profiles.avatar_url`.
  Merging the PR does not apply it; application and post-deploy verification
  are the separate next step.
- Save ordering is upload new object, update profile, then delete the obsolete
  custom object. Failed profile updates compensate by deleting the new object;
  failed post-update cleanup preserves the new profile state and surfaces a
  warning.
- VERIFY & SHIP preflight on project `pijnmcllmfgjmgsvtcej` found 10 empty
  `avatar_url` values and 1 `/avatar/calice.svg`, zero values incompatible with
  the new CHECK, no pre-existing `avatar-profili` bucket and no pre-existing
  `avatar_profili_*` policies.
- Final local verification with Bun 1.3.14 passed: lint with 14 warnings (13
  pre-existing plus the deliberate `<img>` for blob/Storage avatar URLs) and no
  errors, typecheck, 556 tests with zero failures, build and `git diff --check`.
  The `frontend-next` CI floor and its regression contract are aligned from
  538 to the verified 556 tests. Legacy frontend and backend were not run
  locally; they are not modified.
- Deliberate historical verification residues remain: one test bottle in state
  `aperta`, the test account, and three objects in each of its `cantina` and
  `annunci` folders.

